🚀 Getting Started with Shell Scripting in Linux

💡 What is Shell Scripting?
 Shell scripting is simply writing Linux commands in a file to automate repetitive tasks. Instead of typing commands one by one, you run them all at once.

Think of it as moving from manual mode → autopilot mode 🛫.

🔹 Shell Script Basics
1️⃣ Shebang (interpreter line):
      #!/bin/bash

2️⃣ Variables:
      name="Example"
      echo "Hello, $name"

3️⃣ Taking Input:
       read user
       echo "Welcome, $user!"

4️⃣ Conditions (if/else):
      if [ $1 -gt 10 ]; then
      echo "Number is greater than 10"
      else
      echo "Number is 10 or less"
      fi

5️⃣ Loops:
      for i in 1 2 3
      do
       echo "Looping... number $i"
      done

6️⃣ Functions:
      greet () {
      echo "Hello from a function!"
      }
      greet

7️⃣ Make script executable & run:
      chmod +x script.sh
      ./script.sh
